    "scope": "Two useful Commons2025 west-front and2019 aerial exterior photographs plus standard viewer PMTiles/DEM. Reference photographs viewed only, not downloaded/redistributed. No bespoke drawings/surveys researched.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2025-05-17_Saint_Gregory_the_Illuminator_Cathedral,_Yerevan.jpg",
        "image": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/28/2025-05-17_Saint_Gregory_the_Illuminator_Cathedral%2C_Yerevan.jpg",
        "author": "Alexey Komarov / Alexkom000",
        "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected17May2025 west front: pale warm tan stone panel faces, broad main roof and tall rear polygonal drum/cone/cross, two lower chapel cupolas, projecting middle entrance and belfry. Large recessed round entry/vault with nested arches, flanking stacked arched windows and lower doors; paired long upper slots and relief crosses. Facet-front triangular pediments form a zigzag cornice below the brown stone cones. Broad approach stairs/plaza visible but not surveyed. Photograph viewed only, not redistributed."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Gregory_the_Illuminator_Cathedral_from_air,_April_2019.jpg",
        "image": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ec/Saint_Gregory_the_Illuminator_Cathedral_from_air%2C_April_2019.jpg",
        "author": "Aleksey Chalabyan / Xelgen",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected8April2019 aerial exterior: high rear main church with very steep stone roof planes, broad polygonal drum with paired rectangular slits and faceted cone; lower north/south chapels have hipped bases and smaller polygonal drums/cones. Projecting west gate/bell shaft has tall paired slots, octagonal small cupola and open deep lower vault; two-story narthex between chapels has flat roof with a small blue polygonal skylight. Lower side windows are stacked in vertical recesses; main outer piers are thick rectangular stone masses. Current PMTiles footprint controls the complete envelope; internal partitions, cupola centers/heights, window rhythm and stairs are picture estimates. No reference photograph redistributed, and no bespoke plan/survey researched."
      }
    ]
